      "prompt": "Review a Nano floor-to-table controller after an RGB-guided trial stopped while holding green. The calibrated head and wrist pixels and 17 encoders gave the following approximate body-frame measurements: rim distance 0.3075 m, tangent span [-0.1867,0.2318] m, prior blue center [0.3375,0.1217] m, desired tangent 0.1610 m, desired inset 0.085 m. Current candidate tangent offsets in metres are [0,0.08,-0.08,0.115,-0.115,0.15,-0.15]. No existing candidate was both reachable and at least 0.078 m from the previously placed cube. The box is 40 mm wide. How should the program discretize the visible free space after its normal candidates fail? Propose a fallback lateral grid spacing between 5 and 35 millimetres and an optional extra depth between 0 and 30 millimetres, with a brief rationale. Keep clearance, original minimum inset, URDF limits, motor guard and all scoring rules unchanged. Proposals are checked with IK before motion.",
