      "rationale": "Use a 20 mm lateral lattice (half the 40 mm cube width), anchored on the nominal tangent, so the unsampled 35 mm gaps and the just-missed 78 mm clearance boundary are covered without an excessive number of IK checks. Add one optional 20 mm deeper inset ring: relative to the prior cube at 30 mm inset, radial separation rises from 55 mm to 75 mm, giving about 84.7 mm center distance at the nominal tangent and clearing 78 mm. The original 85 mm minimum inset is only increased, and every grid point is still subject to the unchanged URDF, motor-guard, and IK checks before motion.",
